    "title": "pandas.DatetimeIndex.month — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DatetimeIndex.month#\n\n- property DatetimeIndex.month[source]#\n- The month as January=1, December=12. See also \n  - `DatetimeIndex.year`\n  - The year of the datetime.\n  - `DatetimeIndex.day`\n  - The day of the datetime.\n Examples >>> datetime_series = pd.Series( ... pd.date_range(\"2000-01-01\", periods=3, freq=\"ME\") ... ) >>> datetime_series 0 2000-01-31 1 2000-02-29 2 2000-03-31 dtype: datetime64[us] >>> datetime_series.dt.month 0 1 1 2 2 3 dtype: int32",
    "markdown_length": 465,
